    "subject": "Geography",
    "chapter_number": 7,
    "chapter_name": "Life Lines of National Economy",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Why are the means of transportation and communication called the lifelines of a nation and its economy?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The means of transportation and communication are called the lifelines of a nation and its economy due to the reasons given below:\n→ The means of transportation and communication help in the production and movement of goods and services.\n→ Transport helps in the development of communication. Various means of communication help us in interacting with others in all parts of the world. It has brought the world closer.\n→ Transport like railways help us in conducting various activities like business, sightseeing, pilgrimage, and transportation of goods over longer distances.\n→ Pipelines are used for transporting crude oil and natural gas to refineries and factories.\n→ Water provides the cheapest means of transport and is useful for international trade.\n→ Air transport provides the fastest, most comfortable mode of transport.\nThus, it is clear that there are many advantages of transportation and communication. These means help in the development of the country. So they are called the lifelines of a nation and its economy.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, it is clear that there are many advantages of transportation and communication, making them the lifelines of a nation and its economy.",
